  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on variance as a formal measure of risk, preferring the lottery with higher variance (Lottery B). The individual considers the difference in outcomes and explicitly accepts the risk of getting nothing in order to have a chance at a higher gain, which aligns with a preference for higher variability in outcomes. While the individual does not mention 'variance' as a statistical concept, their reasoning centers on the core idea behind variance — the spread of outcomes and willingness to accept uncertainty for higher upside. The information considered (potential gain, risk, chance of higher payoff) overlaps with the informational basis of the variance-based reason. The justification (choosing risk for higher reward) matches the directional preference of the reason (favoring higher variance). Although the reasoning is expressed in intuitive, non-technical terms rather than statistical analysis, the underlying logic corresponds closely to the variance-based decision rule.",
